.SH NAME
.PP
gemini-markets-stream-orders - Stream order updates (authenticated)


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBgemini-markets stream orders [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Stream real-time order updates for your account.

.PP
Requires API credentials. Shows order status changes including:
accepted, booked, fill, canceled/cancelled, closed, rejected

.PP
Examples:
  # All order events
  gemini-markets stream orders

.PP
# Only fills (executions)
  gemini-markets stream orders --event-type fill

.PP
# Only specific symbols
  gemini-markets stream orders --symbol GEMI-FED260318-MAINTAIN

.PP
# Multiple filters
  gemini-markets stream orders --symbol GEMI-BTC* --event-type fill,booked

.PP
# Only orders from this session
  gemini-markets stream orders --session-only


.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB--event-type\fP=[]
	filter by event type(s): accepted, booked, fill, canceled/cancelled, closed, rejected

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for orders

.PP
\fB--session-only\fP[=false]
	only show orders from current session

.PP
\fB--symbol\fP=[]
	filter by symbol(s), supports wildcards (e.g., GEMI-BTC*)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--no-websocket\fP[=false]
	disable WebSocket and use REST API only

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="json"
	output format: json, table, or csv

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress stderr output for pure JSON piping

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	output compact JSON without pretty-printing

.PP
\fB--sandbox\fP[=false]
	use sandbox environment

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30
	request timeout in seconds

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	use full field names in JSON output (default: abbreviated)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gemini-markets stream orders
  gemini-markets stream orders --event-type fill --symbol GEMI-BTC*
  gemini-markets stream orders --session-only -q
.EE


